In the `main` function, we define two function pointers - `enqueue_ptr` and `dequeue_ptr` - that point to the `enqueue` and `dequeue` functions, respectively. This allows us to pass these functions as arguments to other functions, and allows us to switch between different implementations of these functions at runtime.
